# Certificate in AI – Course Web App

A centralized **static web application** for the *Certificate in AI* course, built collaboratively by our team. It will bring the course content (modules, sessions, resources and exercises) together in one easy-to-browse site.

## Tech
- Static site: HTML, CSS and JavaScript only (no backend or database)
- Can be hosted on any static host (e.g. GitHub Pages, Netlify)

## Getting Started
1. Clone the repository.
2. Open `index.html` in your browser (or use a simple local server such as `python -m http.server`).

## Working as a Team
> **Important: create a separate branch for your work.**
> Do not commit directly to `main`.

```bash
git checkout -b feature/<your-name>-<short-task>
# make your changes, then
git add .
git commit -m "Short description of your change"
git push -u origin feature/<your-name>-<short-task>
```

Then open a Pull Request into `main` for review before merging.

## Guidelines
- Keep each branch focused on one task or page.
- Pull the latest `main` before starting new work.
- Use clear file names and keep assets in an `assets/` folder.
